tour feature-step-unlink
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note step-unlink <name> <index>: remove the link from one step, so the step reads as a plain step again. The agent reaches for it to undo a wrong link. It is the one way to remove a link (step-link refuses an empty target), and it refuses a step that has no link, so a wrong index shows up as an error instead of silently changing nothing.

